From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:10:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 254/255] dos: patch 0254 -- OPL write pacing per backend: 4 +
 4 status reads on a detected PicoGUS

Every OPL write is followed by 6 dummy status reads after the address and
6 after the data: 12 of a write's 14 port operations. On a 486 each costs
~2 us, so a write is ~29 us, and room 35's densest ISR replay burst (416
writes) holds the SB ISR for ~11-12 ms (dosags lab CAPH-1/1I).

The PicoGUS does not need that spacing (firmware v4.1.1, sw/picogus.cpp):
an address write is a fast write, a data write holds IOCHRDY until the
handler has queued it, and each dummy status read is itself a stretched
cycle. It queues writes in a 256-entry buffer with no full check
(sw/include/cmd_buffers.h), drained once per 128 samples at 49716 Hz
(~2.57 ms), so writes must not arrive much faster: 4 + 4 reads (~20.6 us
per write, ~125 per window) keep half the buffer free even if one drain
is late. Zero reads would overrun it and lose writes.

The pacing is chosen once, at OPL detection, only on a POSITIVE
identification through the card's own control port, as its pgusinit reads
it: knock 0xCC at 0x1D0, magic 0xDD, protocol 4, SB mode (5), OPL base
0x388; an unknown register (0x80) ends control mode. Every other card --
a Creative OPL3, the PicoGUS in another mode, anything unknown -- keeps
6 + 6. On a detected PicoGUS the ISR replay's per-IRQ budget defaults to
448 (448 x 20.6 us = 9.2 ms). Why the probe is safe on a machine without a PicoGUS: it is the card's
own detection sequence, as pgusinit does it on any machine
(pgusinit/pgusinit.c:1307-1314 at v4.1.1: knock, select magic, read
0x1D2); the PicoGUS project chose 0x1D0 because "nothing is listed in
Ralf Brown's Port List" (common/picogus.h:5 -- their statement, not
verified here). On an undecoded port the ISA bus floats (0xFF), so only
two bytes are ever written to 0x1D0 before the probe gives up; a garbage
answer on any later register just fails the match and keeps 6 + 6.
SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_PICOGUS_PROBE=0 skips the probe entirely (a field escape
if some card does decode 0x1D0). The control-mode exit (0x80) reaches
select_picogus()'s default branch, which clears control_active
(sw/picogus.cpp:282-283; 0x80 is not a CMD_ value in common/picogus.h).
SDL_HINT_DOS_OPL_DELAY_READS=N (1..6) and
SDL_HINT_DOS_MIDI_DEFER_MAX_PER_IRQ override either choice.
SDL_DOSOplPacing() reports what was chosen.

RENUMBERED 2026-09-25 from 0228 to 0254 (the coordinator's SDL block 0250-0259),
so the series sorts after main's SDL 0240. It lands on main ahead of the RTC
pump series (SDL 0230-0237), which re-applies on top. 0228 never landed on
main; its slot is retired on lab/journeys.
Re-cut onto main's SDL 0199 (the audio cost diagnostics read the clock only
when on): in SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister this patch's line now sits beside 0199's
gated uclock() diagnostic; the change itself is unchanged.

